# Testing and Quality

- Use Jest + Testing Library for behavior-focused tests; assert user-visible outcomes, not implementation details.
- Cover key dashboard flows: route rendering, loading/error/empty states, and critical data interactions.
- Mock network boundaries (RTK Query/Axios) while keeping component logic realistic.
- Keep tests deterministic and fast; avoid real timers/network and brittle snapshot overuse.
- Ensure TypeScript strictness, ESLint compliance, and Prettier formatting before considering work complete.
- Add or update tests when behavior changes; avoid shipping untested critical paths.
